/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Component: Magnesium chloride (MgCl2, CAS 7786-30-3) -- CASE-LOCAL.

  Authored for the code-to-code
  comparison with NanoFiltran, whose shipped example is a Na+/Mg2+/Cl-
  solution (10/20/50 mol/m3) -- i.e. NaCl 10 + MgCl2 20 mol/m3.  The
  catalogue carries no MgCl2 record; this one carries ONLY what the
  DSPM-DE pore model reads: the identity, the molar mass and the ion
  stoichiometry (the salt is decomposed into its ions through
  `dissociatesTo`, and every transport fact of an ion lives on its
  species record).  No thermochemistry: nothing here prices an energy.
    MW  95.211 g/mol  (24.305 + 2 x 35.453, IUPAC standard atomic weights)
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           MgCl2;
formula        MgCl2;
CAS            7786-30-3;
MW             95.211;          // g/mol  (= kg/kmol)

role           nonvolatile;
dissociation   3;               // van't Hoff factor
dissociatesTo  { Mg 1; Cl 2; }  // ion stoichiometry (formula-like identity)
